StageAble Bridge
=================

StageAble Bridge is the Ableton Live control surface (Remote Script) used by the
StageAble application. It is a trimmed and rebranded fork of AbletonOSC.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AbletonOSC
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:   https://github.com/ideoforms/AbletonOSC
Based on:   commit 0ca68214bd62c9b5cb641ca34006cfd70ba94430
License:    MIT (see ./LICENSE)
Copyright:  Daniel John Jones and contributors

Modifications made in this fork:
  - Trimmed to only the Song and Track handlers plus the OSC server plumbing
    (application/clip/clip_slot/device/scene/view/midimap handlers removed).
  - Added StageAble batched endpoints in song.py / track.py:
      /live/song/get/meter_at_beats
      /live/song/get/name
      /live/song/get/file_path
      /live/track/get/arrangement_clips/name_chunk
      /live/track/set/arrangement_clips/name
  - Renamed package, logger, and log file to StageAble Bridge.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
python-osc (bundled in ./pythonosc)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream:   https://github.com/attwad/python-osc
License:    Public Domain (Unlicense)

This bundled copy is vendored from AbletonOSC and is used by the OSC server so
the control surface has no external dependencies inside Live's Python runtime.
